# Standards

- TypeScript in `apps/web`. Python 3.11+ in `services/engine`, `services/knowledge`, `services/agent`, `services/optimisation`, `services/discovery`, `services/progression`, and `services/endgame`. The Lua adapter stays small and talks JSON lines.
- Match the existing layout. Do not add a second web framework or a second calculation engine.
- Keep secrets out of the repo. API keys belong in an uncommitted local config.
- Prefer the pinned upstream Path of Building checkout over a fork.
- Tests that claim an engine result must launch the real adapter. Unit tests that do not launch it must not assert character stats.
- Comments explain a non-obvious engine constraint, not the next line of code.
- Do not vendor the Path of Building `src/` or `TreeData/` trees. The bootstrap script checks them out.
